//
// Expected: f0a0 at one session, f1a1 at two.
//
// Alice signs a fresh nonce and Bob verifies and uses it. The nonce carries a
// generated value, but nothing ties it to Bob's run: at two sessions the
// attacker replays Alice#2's signed nonce into Bob, and Bob and Bob#2 both
// accept na#2. Freshness asks whether the attacker can keep a value the same
// across sessions and have it accepted again, so it fails, and the duplicate
// acceptance fails the authentication query as well. Freshness once asked
// only whether the value contained a generated constant. At one session
// there is no second flight to replay. freshness_bound_to_challenge.vp is the
// counterweight.
attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private ska
	gka = PUBKEY(ska)
	generates na
	s1 = SIGN(ska, na)
]

Alice -> Bob: [gka], na, s1

principal Bob[
	_ = SIGNVERIF(gka, na, s1)?
	u = HASH(na)
]

queries[
	freshness? na
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: na
]
